<article class="env-lemma" id="0C0C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C0C">Lemma <span data-tag="0C0C">32.8.9</span>.</a> Notation and assumptions as in Situation <a href="/tag/081D" data-tag="081D">32.8.1</a>. If </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is smooth, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f_0$ is locally of finite presentation, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then $f_ i$ is smooth for some $i \geq 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Being smooth is local on the source and the target (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01V6" data-tag="01V6">29.35.2</a>) hence we may assume $S_0, X_0, Y_0$ affine (details omitted). The corresponding algebra fact is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C0B" data-tag="0C0B">10.168.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>